<tmc-service-inc>
<pub id="RM0550J">
<servcat id="10">
<name>Body &amp; Electrical</name>
<section id="1002O_S0008" variety="S0008">
<name>Engine Immobiliser</name>
<ttl id="1002O_S0008_741KM_T000P" variety="T000P">
<name>Engine Immobiliser System</name>
<para id="RM000000MGV00OX" category="C" type-id="3055Z" name-id="580M3-00" from="200612">
<dtccode>B2779</dtccode>
<dtcname>Engine Starter Communication Malfunction</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM000000MGV00OX_04" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000A4500000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>The certification ECU (smart key computer assembly) stores this code when the remote start (Toyota genuine) does not respond or when the codes do not match even though the remote start is ON.</ptxt>
<ptxt>The DTC is cleared when communication with the remote start is established and ends normally; past DTCs are not stored.</ptxt>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.00in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="3.00in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="3.08in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC No.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC Detection Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Inspection Area</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>B2779</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Remote start does not respond, communication malfunction</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Remote start (Toyota genuine)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Certification ECU (Smart Key Computer Assembly)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Wire Harness and Connector</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
<atten4>
<ptxt>B2779 applies only to vehicles with remote start (Toyota genuine).</ptxt>
</atten4>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000000MGV00OX_05" type-id="51" category="05" proc-id="RM0550J___0000A4600000">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<atten3>
<ptxt>When replacing the certification ECU (smart key computer assembly), check the precautions (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM000000MGE00SX"/>) and the registration procedure in the reference section before proceeding.</ptxt>
</atten3>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000000MGV00OX_06" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM000000MGV00OX_06_0005" proc-id="RM0550J___0000A4700000">
<testtitle>Re-register Remote Start</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), re-register the remote start.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>Engine can be started with remote start</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000000MGV00OX_06_0008" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000000MGV00OX_06_0007" fin="false">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000000MGV00OX_06_0007" proc-id="RM0550J___0000A4800000">
<testtitle>Inspect Wire Harness and Connector (Certification ECU - Remote Start ECU)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<atten4>
<ptxt>Only the tester connection numbers between the certification ECU and accessory bus buffer are given; for the tester connection numbers between the accessory bus buffer and remote start ECU, refer to the accessory manual.</ptxt>
</atten4>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="B156220J03" width="2.775699831in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
<test1>
<ptxt>Disconnect the certification ECU (smart key computer assembly) connector and the accessory bus buffer.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between each terminal (between the certification ECU and remote start ECU) of the vehicle side wire harness connectors.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.10in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="0.96in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.07in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
<ptxt>(Certification ECU - Accessory Bus Buffer)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>27(CANH) - 1(CAN+)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>28(CANL) - 2(CAN-)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
<table>
<title>Resistance</title>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.08in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="0.96in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.09in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
<ptxt>(Accessory Bus Buffer - Remote Start ECU)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>1 (CAN+) - Refer to accessory manual</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>2 (CAN-) - Refer to accessory manual</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
<table>
<title>Resistance</title>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.08in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="0.96in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.09in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
<ptxt>(Accessory Bus Buffer)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>3 (GND) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
<table>
<title>Resistance</title>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="2.08in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="0.96in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.09in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
<ptxt>(Verification ECU)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>28 (CANH) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>10k Ω or higher</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>27 (CANL) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
